step Coarse Blasting Powder to 94 · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Coarse Blasting Powder is orange at 75 (yellow 85, green 90, grey 95): about 30 crafts to 94, up to 38 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Coarse Stone. One Coarse Stone a craft (Tin Veins).
  craft 3929 until 94

step Copper Tube to 100 · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Copper Tube is yellow at 94 (yellow 80, green 95, grey 110): about 14 crafts to 100, up to 20 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 2 Copper Bar and 1 Weak Flux. Two Copper Bars and a Weak Flux a craft (blacksmithing and engineering suppliers). Needs an anvil nearby. If you got here without learning Copper Tube, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 3924
  craft 3924 until 100

step Engineering recipes at 100
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Practice Lock (from 100) and Silver Contact (from 90).
  learn 8334
  learn 3973

step Practice Lock to 125 · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Practice Lock is orange at 100 (yellow 115, green 122, grey 130): about 31 crafts to 125, up to 36 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Bronze Bar, 2 Handful of Copper Bolts and 1 Weak Flux. Make the 12 Handful of Copper Bolts first. Use the 50 Handful of Copper Bolts you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. Practice Locks sell to rogues, or open them yourself. Needs an anvil nearby. If you got here without learning Handful of Copper Bolts, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 3922
  craft 3922 x12
  craft 8334 until 125

step Engineering recipes at 125
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Heavy Blasting Powder (from 125).
  learn 3945

step Heavy Blasting Powder to 144 · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Heavy Blasting Powder is yellow at 125 (yellow 125, green 135, grey 145): about 52 crafts to 144, up to 70 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Heavy Stone. One Heavy Stone a craft (Iron Deposits). Keep some: Iron Grenades take one each.
  craft 3945 until 144

step Engineering recipes at 144
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Big Bronze Bomb (from 140).
  learn 3950

step Big Bronze Bomb to 150 · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Big Bronze Bomb is yellow at 144 (yellow 140, green 165, grey 190): about 7 crafts to 150, up to 9 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 2 Heavy Blasting Powder, 3 Bronze Bar and 1 Silver Contact and makes 3. Make the 10 Silver Contact (2 crafts) first. Use the 14 Heavy Blasting Powder you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data. Needs an anvil nearby. Engineering 150 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 3973 x2
  craft 3950 until 150
  skill Engineering 150

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Expert (150-225)
section Engineering 150-225

step Expert Engineering
  tip Expert raises the cap from 150 to 225 for 50s (Classic's price; Forever's is not in the data); it needs Engineering 125 and character level 20, so you can take it on any visit from 125. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Springspindle Fizzlegear (Ironforge); Horde Roxxik (Orgrimmar). This route trains it at Springspindle Fizzlegear (Ironforge) for the Alliance and Roxxik (Orgrimmar) for the Horde, who also teach the recipes of 150-225: one trainer for every visit. Learn now: Aquadynamic Fish Attractor (from 150) and Bronze Framework (from 145). 150-225 takes about 31s of vendor goods, plus 25 Medium Leather, 25 Wool Cloth, 128 Bronze Bar, 6 Silver Bar, 81 Iron Bar, 22 Mithril Bar and 390 Solid Stone to gather or buy.
