step Aquadynamic Fish Attractor to 166 · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Aquadynamic Fish Attractor is yellow at 150 (yellow 150, green 160, grey 170): about 31 crafts to 166, up to 39 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 2 Bronze Bar, 1 Nightcrawlers and 1 Coarse Blasting Powder and makes 3. Make the 1 Coarse Blasting Powder first. Use the 30 Coarse Blasting Powder you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. Nightcrawlers come from trade and fishing suppliers; the attractors sell to fishermen. If you got here without learning Coarse Blasting Powder, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 3929
  craft 3929 x1
  craft 9271 until 166

step Bronze Framework to 175 · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Bronze Framework is yellow at 166 (yellow 145, green 170, grey 195): about 19 crafts to 175, up to 25 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 2 Bronze Bar, 1 Medium Leather and 1 Wool Cloth. Bronze Frameworks are parts for later gadgets; the extras sell to vendors.
  craft 3953 until 175

step Engineering recipes at 175
  tip Back to Springspindle Fizzlegear (Ironforge) (Alliance) or Roxxik (Orgrimmar) (Horde): Solid Blasting Powder (from 175).
  learn 12585 npc 5174 only Alliance
  learn 12585 npc 11017 only Horde

step Solid Blasting Powder to 195 · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Solid Blasting Powder is yellow at 175 (yellow 175, green 185, grey 195): about 72 crafts to 195, up to 103 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 2 Solid Stone. Two Solid Stone a craft (Mithril Deposits). Make plenty: the triggers, slugs and Gyro-Shot all use it.
  craft 12585 until 195

step Engineering recipes at 195
  tip Back to Springspindle Fizzlegear (Ironforge) (Alliance) or Roxxik (Orgrimmar) (Horde): Big Iron Bomb (from 190).
  learn 3967 npc 5174 only Alliance
  learn 3967 npc 11017 only Horde

step Big Iron Bomb to 210 · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Big Iron Bomb is yellow at 195 (yellow 190, green 210, grey 230): about 22 crafts to 210, up to 27 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 3 Iron Bar, 3 Heavy Blasting Powder and 1 Silver Contact and makes 2. Make the 28 Heavy Blasting Powder and 25 Silver Contact (5 crafts) first. Use the 38 Heavy Blasting Powder you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. A Silver Bar makes five Silver Contacts (grey by now: no points, but no trip to a vendor either); the Heavy Blasting Powder comes from Heavy Stone. Each craft makes two bombs. Specialisation (optional): at 200 and character level 30, Springspindle Fizzlegear (Ironforge), Lilliam Sparkspindle (Stormwind), Graham Van Talen (Undercity) or Tinkerwiz (Ratchet) sends you to Gnomish Engineering (Tinkmaster Overspark, Ironforge, or Oglethorpe Obnoticus, Booty Bay: 6 Mithril Tubes, an Accurate Scope and 2 Advanced Target Dummies) or Goblin Engineering (Nixx Sprocketspring, Gadgetzan: 20 Big Iron Bombs, 20 Solid Dynamite and 5 Explosive Sheep). The Accurate Scope schematic now binds when picked up, but the quest takes a scope someone else made. The membership card lasts 14 days of play; renewing it costs 2g. You can take only one; neither is needed for 300, and the beta never tested them (it stopped at level 30). Needs an anvil nearby. If you got here without learning Heavy Blasting Powder and Silver Contact, learn them now: an earlier step teaches them.
  learn 3945
  learn 3973
  craft 3945 x28
  craft 3973 x5
  craft 3967 until 210

step Engineering recipes at 210
  tip Back to Springspindle Fizzlegear (Ironforge) (Alliance) or Roxxik (Orgrimmar) (Horde): Hi-Impact Mithril Slugs (from 210).
  learn 12596 npc 5174 only Alliance
  learn 12596 npc 11017 only Horde

step Hi-Impact Mithril Slugs to 225 · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Hi-Impact Mithril Slugs is yellow at 210 (yellow 210, green 230, grey 250): about 19 crafts to 225, up to 22 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Mithril Bar and 1 Solid Blasting Powder and makes 200. Use the 19 Solid Blasting Powder you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. One Mithril Bar and one Solid Blasting Powder a craft; hunters buy the slugs. Needs an anvil nearby. Engineering 225 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 12596 until 225
  skill Engineering 225

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Artisan (225-300)
section Engineering 225-300

step Artisan Engineering
  tip Artisan raises the cap from 225 to 300 for 4g 50s (Classic's price; Forever's is not in the data); it needs Engineering 200 and character level 35, so you can take it on any visit from 200. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Buzzek Bracketswing (Tanaris); Horde Buzzek Bracketswing (Tanaris). This route trains it at Buzzek Bracketswing (Tanaris) for the Alliance and Buzzek Bracketswing (Tanaris) for the Horde, who also teach the recipes of 225-300: one trainer for every visit. 225-300 takes about 2g 80s of recipes, plus 145 Mithril Bar, 174 Thorium Bar and 26 Runecloth to gather or buy.
